Hometown packages (tools/hometown, cities/pkg)
----------------------------------------------
  A Hometown package (?city=pkg&pkg=<id>) is a place compiled by tools/hometown/compile.py from open map data. The
  compiler is part of this repository (MIT); the packages it writes are derived databases and keep their sources'
  terms. Each package's manifest.json lists its sources, their versions and these credits:
  - (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License 1.0 (https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright): the road
    network (names, classes, one-ways), water and land use, and the OpenStreetMap-derived building footprints, read
    through Overture Maps. A package's geodata.js is an ODbL derived database.
  - Overture Maps Foundation (https://overturemaps.org), CDLA Permissive 2.0 / ODbL 1.0 by theme: the buildings theme
    (footprints and heights, including Microsoft, Google and Esri contributions), the places theme.
  - USGS 3D Elevation Program, 1/3 arc-second DEM: US government work, public domain.
  - tools/hometown/osm/osm-roads-us.parquet (the compiler's lane side table: lanes, widths, one-ways, speed limits
    by OSM way id): (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License 1.0, a derived database made from Geofabrik's
    US extract by tools/hometown/osm_roads.py. NOT covered by the MIT License in LICENSE. See tools/hometown/osm/NOTICE.md.
  The game shows the credit on the map (cities/pkg/js/pkg-hud.js) and on its Credits page (wagmi/credits.js). No
  brand name is shown: businesses are named by what they are and the street they stand on.
